WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.112
It was a cold winter morning in Prickly Pear.

2
00:00:04.113 --> 00:00:06.529
Deputy Cleo was in a hurry.

3
00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:12.544
She ran into the office, where Sheriff Roscoe was sipping hot coffee.

4
00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:16.158
"You'll have to work without me today," Cleo said.

5
00:00:16.159 --> 00:00:20.113
Roscoe grinned. "How did I get so lucky?"

6
00:00:20.114 --> 00:00:23.666
That dog loved teasing his deputy.

7
00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.819
Cleo rolled her eyes.

8
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:31.125
"Annie is sick, so I'm teaching school today. I'll see you tomorrow."

9
00:00:31.126 --> 00:00:41.871
Cleo hurried off so fast she didn't notice Roscoe's worried look.

10
00:00:41.872 --> 00:00:46.443
The students were waiting inside the schoolhouse.

11
00:00:46.444 --> 00:00:50.368
A potbellied stove kept the classroom warm.

12
00:00:50.369 --> 00:00:53.004
"Good morning!" Cleo said.

13
00:00:53.005 --> 00:00:57.452
"Miss Annie doesn't feel well. So I'll be your teacher today."

14
00:00:57.453 --> 00:01:03.989
Sarah raised her paw. "Is Miss Annie okay?"

15
00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:07.017
"She has a bad cold," Cleo said.

16
00:01:07.018 --> 00:01:10.888
"But she'll be okay."

17
00:01:10.889 --> 00:01:15.653
"It'll be fun having Deputy Cleo teach us," Oswald said.

18
00:01:15.654 --> 00:01:20.401
The other students cheered.

19
00:01:20.402 --> 00:01:24.835
Cleo blushed. "What should we do first?"

20
00:01:24.836 --> 00:01:28.875
"We always start with math," Lizzie said.

21
00:01:28.876 --> 00:01:34.224
Cleo frowned. She hadn't liked math back when she was in school.

22
00:01:34.225 --> 00:01:37.256
In fact, she still didn't like it.

23
00:01:37.257 --> 00:01:40.787
But luckily that kitty had an idea.

24
00:01:40.788 --> 00:01:44.837
"Let's talk about numbers," Cleo said.

25
00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:47.211
"I used to live in a big city.

26
00:01:47.212 --> 00:01:50.920
More than twenty thousand folks lived there."

27
00:01:50.921 --> 00:01:54.123
She wrote the number on the chalkboard.

28
00:01:54.124 --> 00:01:56.900
"The city had three train stops.

29
00:01:56.901 --> 00:02:00.460
There were four hotels and six restaurants.

30
00:02:00.461 --> 00:02:04.137
My apartment building had ten floors."

31
00:02:04.138 --> 00:02:07.958
Cleo wrote these numbers down too.

32
00:02:07.959 --> 00:02:11.112
Then she pointed to the chalkboard.

33
00:02:11.113 --> 00:02:14.651
"Look at these fancy numbers!"

34
00:02:14.652 --> 00:02:17.713
Those youngsters were mighty pleased.

35
00:02:17.714 --> 00:02:22.538
Their new teacher wasn't giving them any math problems to solve!

36
00:02:22.539 --> 00:02:25.998
"That's enough math," Cleo said.

37
00:02:25.999 --> 00:02:32.811
"Woo-hoo!" The students grinned at each other.

38
00:02:32.812 --> 00:02:38.621
Roscoe paced back and forth in the office.

39
00:02:38.622 --> 00:02:43.297
Poor Miss Annie! She needed someone to take care of her.

40
00:02:43.298 --> 00:02:45.344
He scratched his chin.

41
00:02:45.345 --> 00:02:49.173
When he was sick, he liked something hot to eat.

42
00:02:49.174 --> 00:02:56.719
"That's it!" he thought. "I'll make some potato soup."

43
00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:06.212
The sheriff raced to the boardinghouse kitchen.

44
00:03:06.213 --> 00:03:10.710
He put potatoes, onions, and milk on the counter.

45
00:03:10.711 --> 00:03:14.975
He found a big pot.

46
00:03:14.976 --> 00:03:17.460
Roscoe peeled the potatoes.

47
00:03:17.461 --> 00:03:19.901
The peels flew everywhere.

48
00:03:19.902 --> 00:03:25.202
He chopped the potatoes and dumped them in the pot.

49
00:03:25.203 --> 00:03:32.600
Then he added milk.

50
00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:38.918
Next he chopped the onions. "Whew! My eyes are watering."

51
00:03:38.919 --> 00:03:42.858
He took out his handkerchief and wiped his eyes.

52
00:03:42.859 --> 00:03:47.199
The handkerchief slipped from his paw and fell in the pot.

53
00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:56.922
"Oh no!" Roscoe watched in shock as the handkerchief sank into the soup.

